//! Letter-bigram tables for the wrong-layout word test (`convert::is_wrong_layout`, #147).
//!
//! `X_COSTS[a][b]` is the cost of letter `b` following letter `a` inside a word:
//! `round(-16 * log2 P(b | a))`, clamped to 255 (so 16 units are one bit). Index 0 is the word
//! boundary (row 0: the first letter, column 0: the end of a word); 1.. are the lowercase letters
//! `a`–`z` (English) and `а`–`я` (Russian, `ё` folded into `е`), in alphabet order.
//!
//! Source: the 50,000 most frequent words of each language in FrequencyWords by Hermit Dave
//! (<https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords>, 2018 OpenSubtitles lists `en_50k.txt` and
//! `ru_50k.txt`, content CC BY-SA 4.0). Each word counts with the square root of its frequency
//! (so common words matter more without drowning the rest); characters outside the alphabet split
//! a word; add-k smoothing with k = 1e-5 of the row total. Generated once; only the numbers are kept.

